SHARED SOFTWARE AND INDEPENDENT ASSEMBLY
The generic projection uniforms, projection GLSL and projMaterial helper were adapted from styles/white-model/demo/studio.js into projection.js. This reuse covers material behaviour only; no original makeStudio/build/buildCity or main/story renderer is called. Generic text/readout/pin/rangeLine/subtitle/scrim primitives from styles/white-model/demo/overlay.js are reused; its original endCard is not called. Core math and core/three/post.js supply generic deterministic interpolation, GTAO, physical DOF, bloom and vignette. Shared toolkit copyright 2026 LemoLab, MIT; full notice in TOOLKIT_LICENSE.txt.
New files geometry.js, room.js, light.js, hud.js and film.js independently assemble the model, room, native Three.js lights/camera, all layer timing, world-anchored scene annotations and recreated end card. Camera.json stores measured reference compositions as data. Three.js including RoomEnvironment is MIT. No original movie frames, generated imagery or original audio are production assets.

